    {
      "id": "claim_73a47b84e8974620adb6854308a26a4c",
      "statement": "Both GRPO policy paths score the terminal latent z_K with the shared unconditional realism reward (RewardModel, mode-agnostic PatchGAN trained on partial-denoise preference pairs). For the ControlNet path the unconditional FID callback is suppressed post-merge via TrainingSpine.run(..., forbidden_callbacks={\"fid\": ...}, forbidden_monitors={\"val/fid\": ...}), so a YAML or --callbacks override cannot re-enable it and checkpoint selection uses val/mean_reward.",
      "evidence": [
